{"step_index":692,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T07:02:58Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-07T08:02:58+01:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-07T08:02:59+01:00\nShowing lines 1-35 of 196\n1: # AegisShield EDR & Network AdBlocker: Command & API Reference\n2: \n3: ## 1. Batch File Launchers\n4: \n5: All batch files are located in the project root directory and can be executed via Command Prompt, PowerShell, or Windows File Explorer:\n6: \n7: | Batch File | Description | Execution Command |\n8: | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n9: | **`start_all.bat`** | Launches both the EDR Cyber Dashboard (`:8888`) and the AdBlock Intercepting Proxy (`:8080`) in synchronized background windows. | `.\\start_all.bat` |\n10: | **`start_dashboard.bat`** | Starts only the AegisShield EDR Dashboard and REST/WebSocket API server on `127.0.0.1:8888`. | `.\\start_dashboard.bat` |\n11: | **`start_adblocker.bat`** | Starts only the high-speed AdBlock Intercepting Proxy on `127.0.0.1:8080`. | `.\\start_adblocker.bat` |\n12: | **`run_tests.bat`** | Executes the automated diagnostic testing engine verifying all 22 subsystem health checks. | `.\\run_tests.bat` |\n13: | **`generate_screenshots.bat`** | Executes the high-definition Pillow screenshot engine, producing 10 UI captures in `screenshots/`. | `.\\generate_screenshots.bat` |\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 2. AegisShield CLI Scanner Reference (`cli_scanner.py`)\n18: \n19: The unified CLI tool `cli_scanner.py` provides direct terminal access to all EDR detection, eradication, network origin tracing, policy management, and reporting features.\n20: \n21: ### 2.1 Threat Detection & Remediation\n22: ```bash\n23: # Perform an immediate scan of all running processes\n24: python cli_scanner.py --scan\n25: \n26: # Scan processes and automatically terminate all CRITICAL threats (Score >= 70)\n27: python cli_scanner.py --scan --kill\n28: \n29: # Perform deep PE header and entropy analysis on suspicious binaries during scan\n30: python cli_scanner.py --scan --deep-pe\n31: \n32: # Terminate a specific process by PID immediately\n33: python cli_scanner.py --kill-pid 8412\n34: ```\n35: "}
