{"step_index":696,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T07:03:10Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-07T08:03:10+01:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-07T08:03:10+01:00\nShowing lines 85-135 of 198\n85: python cli_scanner.py --simulate encoded_cmdline\n86: python cli_scanner.py --simulate rmm_beacon\n87: ```\n88: \n89: ---\n90: \n91: ## 3. REST API Reference\n92: \n93: The AegisShield backend exposes a comprehensive RESTful API on `http://127.0.0.1:8888`:\n94: \n95: ### 3.1 Threat & Process Endpoints\n96: | Endpoint | Method | Description | Sample Query / Body |\n97: | :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |\n98: | `/api/scan` | `GET` | Returns list of all evaluated processes with threat scores and indicators. | `GET /api/scan` |\n99: | `/api/kill/{pid}` | `POST` | Immediately terminates process tree and quarantines binary. | `POST /api/kill/8412` |\n100: | `/api/rmm-tools` | `GET` | Returns list of active remote desktop and dual-use RMM tools. | `GET /api/rmm-tools` |\n101: | `/api/persistence` | `GET` | Returns startup, registry, and scheduled task persistence items. | `GET /api/persistence` |\n102: | `/api/simulate-threat` | `POST` | Spawns a harmless threat simulation scenario. | `{\"scenario\": \"temp_trojan\"}` |\n103: | `/api/audit-log` | `GET` | Returns historical record of all remediation and policy actions. | `GET /api/audit-log` |\n104: \n105: ### 3.2 Network Tracer Endpoints\n106: | Endpoint | Method | Description | Sample Query / Body |\n107: | :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |\n108: | `/api/network-processes` | `GET` | Returns all processes using network sockets with mapped remote IPs. | `GET /api/network-processes` |\n109: | `/api/trace-ip` | `GET` | Resolves reverse DNS, ASN, ISP and genuineness score for an IP. | `GET /api/trace-ip?ip=8.8.8.8` |\n110: \n111: ### 3.3 AdBlocker & Web Analytics Endpoints\n112: | Endpoint | Method | Description | Sample Query / Body |\n113: | :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |\n114: | `/api/adblock/status` | `GET` | Returns proxy state (`active`, port, filtered domains count, system proxy state). | `GET /api/adblock/status` |\n115: | `/api/adblock/toggle-proxy`| `POST` | Enables or disables Windows system-wide proxy settings in Registry. | `{\"enabled\": true}` |\n116: | `/api/adblock/traffic-logs`| `GET` | Returns chronological log of browsed websites, categories, and block states. | `GET /api/adblock/traffic-logs?limit=100` |\n117: | `/api/adblock/analytics` | `GET` | Returns aggregated metrics: total requests, blocked ads, bandwidth saved, top sites. | `GET /api/adblock/analytics` |\n118: | `/api/adblock/clear-logs` | `POST` | Flushes web browsing traffic logs. | `POST /api/adblock/clear-logs` |\n119: \n120: ### 3.4 Access Control Policy Endpoints\n121: | Endpoint | Method | Description | Sample Query / Body |\n122: | :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |\n123: | `/api/policy-rules` | `GET` | Returns all allowlist and blocklist rules. | `GET /api/policy-rules` |\n124: | `/api/policy-rules` | `POST` | Creates a new allow or block rule. | `{\"action\": \"allow\", \"type\": \"name\", \"value\": \"code.exe\", \"description\": \"VS Code\"}` |\n125: | `/api/policy-rules/{id}` | `DELETE`| Deletes a rule by ID and removes any associated firewall rules. | `DELETE /api/policy-rules/rule_123` |\n126: \n127: ### 3.5 Email Alerts Endpoints\n128: | Endpoint | Method | Description | Sample Query / Body |\n129: | :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |\n130: | `/api/email/config` | `GET` | Returns current SMTP configuration (passwords masked). | `GET /api/email/config` |\n131: | `/api/email/config` | `POST` | Updates SMTP host, port, TLS, and sender/recipient settings. | `{\"smtp_server\": \"smtp.gmail.com\", ...}` |\n132: | `/api/email/send-report` | `POST` | Triggers immediate compilation and dispatch of executive HTML report. | `POST /api/email/send-report` |\n133: \n134: ---\n135: "}
